{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>Your God has commanded your strength</b> (Psalms 68:29) — 'to the chief musician, of David.' And this 'its strength' is like 'You are the might, O Elohim' (Psalms 68:35). And behold, the meter of עזה is like חקה."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 68, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The Hebrew heading 'לנצח דוד' appears to be a truncated cross-reference or lemma; rendered literally. The comment on meter (משקל) compares the prosodic pattern of עזה to חקה, likely referring to word-final heh as a feminine suffix in both forms."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:33:16.018261492Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}